title: 'fungible: allow deposits below ED into accounts with funds on hold'
doc:
  - audience: [Runtime Dev, Runtime User]
    description: |
      The default `fungible::Unbalanced::increase_balance` and `pallet-balances`' `can_deposit`
      treated any account whose free balance would stay below the existential deposit as a new
      account, even when it had funds on hold. pallet-balances keeps such accounts alive, so this
      was wrong for them. A `BestEffort` deposit returned `Ok(0)` and credited nothing, which is how
      small staking rewards were lost, and `Exact` deposits and transfers failed with
      `BelowMinimum`. Nomination pool members who staked their whole balance could not claim a
      reward below ED, or unbond, since unbond claims pending rewards first.

      An account is now only treated as new when its total balance is zero. New accounts still
      cannot be created below ED.

      Releasing the last hold of an account whose free balance is below ED now passes the dust to
      `handle_raw_dust`. Before, `set_balance_on_hold` dropped it without reducing total issuance.
crates:
  - name: frame-support
    bump: minor
  - name: pallet-balances
    bump: minor
  - name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
    bump: none
